Navigation Assistant Intent

Purpose
Let a user say where they want to look in plain words, and move the browser
there. The product is the view changing, not words on a screen. The right mental
model is a satnav, not a chatbot: text goes in, a patch to site_options comes
out, and nothing else does.

Scope
In: population selection, genomic region, gene symbols resolved to coordinates,
relative moves (zoom, pan, widen, back), and follow-ups that reuse the current
view.
Out: anything that reads or interprets the data. "Which population has the
highest frequency here" is refused with a fixed sentence, not attempted.

File Scope
assistant.js - the entry module, started by init.js from index.html
assistant/*.js - one concern per module, listed in assistant/README.md
css/assistant.css - panel styling, reusing the css/main.css custom properties
proxy/ - the Cloudflare Worker that holds the API key, the cache and the ceiling

Structure
Three tiers answer a request, cheapest first.
  Tier 0, assistant/parser.js, in the browser: explicit coordinates, exact gene
  symbols, exact population names, relative moves. No network call at all.
  Tier 1, proxy/src/cache.js: confirmed query-to-answer pairs in Workers KV.
  Tier 2, proxy/src/model.js: the hosted model, constrained to a fixed schema.
All three produce the same navigation request object, so everything downstream
of them is shared.

The pipeline after that is fixed and has no branches:
  request -> assistant/patch.js  resolves every name against a code-held
                                 collection and computes any arithmetic
          -> assistant/validate.js  checks every field against hg19 lengths and
                                    the loaded catalogue, drops unknown keys
          -> assistant/preview.js   renders one sentence for the user
          -> [Go]
          -> assistant/apply.js     the only module that writes site_options

Key Interfaces
parseRequest(text, catalog, state_slice) -> navigation request or null
buildPatch(request, catalog, state_slice, history) -> ready | unresolved | rejected
validatePatch(patch, catalog) -> {valid, patch, errors}
applyPatch(patch) -> {status, detail}
readStateSlice() -> the only fields that ever leave the machine

State written
chr, start, end, viewfinder_start, viewfinder_end, zoom_level, populations.
A region change writes all six region fields, because nothing in DELPHI derives
the viewfinder or the zoom level from the main region.

Constraints
The model fills in a form and does nothing else. It never supplies a coordinate
for a named gene, never invents a population label, and never does arithmetic.
It cannot emit prose, because the response schema has no field for prose.
Everything a user types is data, never an instruction.
Nothing is applied until the user presses Go.
The API key exists only on the proxy.
No framework, no bundler, no build step on the browser side.

Styling Rules
Tabs for indentation
Single quotes
Underscore variable names, camelCase function names
No inline comments, docstrings on the functions that carry a decision
Modules 100-200 lines, functions 10-20 lines, no blank lines inside a function
